@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Product API
	Testing Koroneiki Product API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal Six                  |
	| Liferay Version 7                   |
	| Liferay Version 6                   |

Scenario: Create and view product
	Koroneiki products created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |

Scenario: Create and view product with properties
	Koroneiki products with properties created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name                    | Liferay Digital Experience Platform |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1                     | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2                     | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3                     | propertyValue3 |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name                    | Liferay Digital Experience Platform |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1                     | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2                     | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3                     | propertyValue3 |

Scenario: Create and view multiple products
	Multiple products created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |

Scenario: Update and view product
	Koroneiki products updated via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: Update and view product with properties
	Koroneiki products with properties updated via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name                    | Liferay Digital Experience Platform |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1                     | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2                     | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3                     | propertyValue3 |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values
	| Name                    | Liferay Portal Six |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp4    | propertyValue4 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp5    | propertyValue5 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp6    | propertyValue6 |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values
	| Name                    | Liferay Portal Six  |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp4     | propertyValue4 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp5     | propertyValue5 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp6     | propertyValue6 |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: Update and view multiple products
	Multiple products updated via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values
	| Name | Liferay Version 7 | |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" to have the following values
	| Name | Liferay Version 6 | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Version 7" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Version 7 | |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Version 6" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Version 6 | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"

Scenario: Remove product and view
	Koroneiki products removed via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: Remove product with properties and view
	Koroneiki products with properties removed via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name                    | Liferay Digital Experience Platform |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1                     | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2                     | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3                     | propertyValue3 |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: Remove multiple products and view
	Multiple products removed via API should not be viewable via API.`

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"

Scenario: Create and view product external link
	Koroneiki product external links created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| External Link Nested Field | liferaydxp                               | |
	| Name                       | Liferay Digital Experience Platform      | |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" via the external link key with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" using the external link domain "liferaydxp" and entity name "LiferayDXP" and entity id "1234"

Scenario: Remove product external link and view
	Koroneiki product external links removed via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"